      },
      "lineNbr": 84,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003571
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-13T23:56:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One more thing, while it is not consistent, we have been moving to not using typedef for structures and rather identifying \"struct foo a_foo;\" rather than \"foo_t a_foo;\". If you choose to keep the typedef, please use the typedef in all places (so note the advantage of using struct foo everywhere, you can declare a struct foo* a_foo in a structure definition without needing access to the typedef).\n\nBeing consistent assures that a grep or cscope finds all the places the struct is used.",
      "revId": "110655858a554265dcda4558a55508a4c6297bd8",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
